<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A product-reviews card: the average score with stars and a review count, the share of reviews per star and a
social-proof footer. A **block** composed from [Rating](<%= page_path(:rating) %>), [Meter](<%= page_path(:meter) %>),
[Separator](<%= page_path(:separator) %>) and AvatarGroup, as on the [Appica homepage](https://appica.dev/ui).

<%= embed Blocks::ReviewSummaryPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
ReviewSummary(rating: product.average_rating, reviews: product.reviews.count) do
  ReviewBreakdown(counts: product.reviews.group(:stars).count, href: ->(stars) { product_reviews_path(product, stars:) })
  ReviewHighlight(avatars: recent_reviewers.map { |user| { src: user.avatar_url, alt: user.name } }) { "Loved by 12,000+ shoppers" }
end
```

- The stars show the exact average (a read-only Rating with `step: 0.1`), in the warning accent.
- `counts:` maps stars to review counts; the percentages are computed from them, highest star first.
- `href:` turns each breakdown row into a link to the filtered reviews.

## Localization

`review_summary.locales.yml` holds the strings: the review count is pluralized per language ("1 verified review",
"4 ověřené recenze", "1.284 ověřených recenzí", Arabic's zero/one/two/few/many forms) and the score, count and
percentages use the locale's number format. `verified: false` drops "verified"; `label:` replaces the line. Switch the
**Locale** display option to try it.

